	abstract = {A robust and well-designed e-government application is the core requirement for the successful implementation of e-government services. Nepal has implemented e-governance in many of its important sectors, and the e-taxation system is one of the primary implementations. Besides normal testing, there are no concrete studies that have been undertaken to uncover the quality of service and user satisfaction of this system. This study analyzes the design quality, user requirements, and overall quality of the e-governance taxation portal of Nepal. In this study, we employ a qualitative research methodology, manual testing, and automated testing to uncover the quality of the portal. Results are evaluated to study the characteristics of software quality requirements as per user needs and ISO\IEC 9126 standard. This study is very important to improvise the quality and maturity level of the e-governance system in Nepal. It provides a huge source of knowledge and supplements the gap in the literature. © 2021, Springer Nature Switzerland AG.},
