	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105045570685?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This study aims to develop a system for the automatic detection and management of ambiguities in software requirement specifications. Ambiguities in requirement specifications can lead to rework and delays in later stages of development, necessitating clarification at the initial stages. Traditional dictionary-based methods struggle to accommodate industry-specific terminology and new concepts, and are insufficient for capturing semantic ambiguities at the sentence level. Therefore, this research employs neuro-symbolic AI, which combines the natural language understanding capabilities of large language models (LLMs) with the logical reasoning abilities of symbolic AI. By using a two-step approach where LLMs extract ambiguous descriptions and symbolic AI validates them, we aim to prevent oversight of ambiguities and improve accuracy. Additionally, drawing on the SECI and IGET models, we incorporate the re-evaluation of ambiguous expressions and the introduction of new perspectives through generative AI to enhance the extraction accuracy of ambiguous expressions in documents. Future plans include evaluating the system using actual requirement specifications and integrating it with knowledge graph systems.  © 2026 IEEE.},
