	abstract = {Customer requirements can not be directly used in design process because they are fuzzy, complex and nonstandard. But customer's expectation to product performance index is embedded in customer requirements. A method based on Vague set theory for fuzzy attributes is discussed, which is to merge and map requirements information obtained from multiple means, in order to get product performance index most concerned by users. Two-stage data fusion algorithm based on Vague set achieves mapping customer requirements to performance index in products design. First, calculate and confirm the weight coefficient for every requirement item; second, calculate the weighted associated offset of requirement-performance in order to sort product performance index by custom's attentions, thus the mapping switch is carried out. The definitions and explains involved in this algorithm are presented, followed an algorithm criterion on its efficacy. This method is efficient in fusing fuzzy customer requirements obtained from multiple means, and in building the products performance index set which the designers should pay more attention to. 1553-9105/ Copyright © 2009 Binary Information Press.},
